# Tailored CV: {{COMPANY}} — {{ROLE}}

> **Source**: derived from `profile/cv.md`, tailored per JD with moderate aggressiveness.
> **Length cap**: 2 pages.
> **Hard rules**: never invent skills/dates/companies/metrics. Weave JD keywords using truth only. Keep one achievement sentence per bullet line; never bunch bullets into inline dot-separated prose.
> **Voice**: keep Nii's voice per `profile/style_guide.md`.

## Structure to produce

```markdown
# Nii Amon Dsane
**[Headline — tailored to JD, 6-10 words]**

[Location • Email • Phone • LinkedIn]

## Summary
[2-4 short sentences or paragraphs. Keep separate ideas on separate lines. Lead with the recommended angle from match_analysis.md. Mirror the JD's must-haves using truth only.]

## Relevant strengths
[5-6 concise bullets aligned to the JD. This is the main tailoring surface alongside the headline and summary.]

## Experience
[Use one Experience section only. List every included role in strict reverse chronological order. Do not split the career into "current" / "earlier" or relevance-based subsections. If the user names a baseline CV, preserve its substantive role bullets unless explicitly told otherwise.]

### [Company] // [Location]
**[Title]** | [Dates]
- [Bullet — outcome-first, metric if available, JD-keyword-aware]
- [Bullet]

## Education
[Standard]

## [Optional: Selected Projects / Speaking / etc. if relevant to JD]
```

## Tailoring rules

1. **Headline** under the name should shift per JD (e.g., "Fintech Engineering Leader" for fintech roles, "Marketplace CTO" for marketplace roles, "AI Product Builder" for AI roles). Must be truth — Nii has done all of these.
2. **Summary** should mirror the JD's must-haves while remaining a concise paragraph.
3. **Relevant strengths** reorders the verified capabilities that best match the JD.
4. **Experience** bullets get rewritten for impact (tighter phrasing, stronger verbs), not invented.
5. **Baseline preservation**: when the user names an existing CV as the baseline, preserve its section structure, role sequence and substantive career bullets. Tailor primarily through headline, summary, relevant strengths, wording and within-role bullet order.
6. **Compression**: only compress or drop career evidence when there is no designated baseline or the user explicitly asks for it.
7. **Metric rules**: reuse from `profile/cv.md` and `profile/achievements.md` only. If a metric is plausible but unsourced, mark `[estimated — verify]`.
8. **ATS weave**: if `meta.json.ats_optimize == true`, weave JD keywords into bullets using truth only.
9. **Readability**: each achievement/responsibility gets its own `-` bullet line. Never merge multiple bullet sentences with `•`, `·`, semicolons or inline separators. If the CV exceeds 2 pages, edit content first, then modestly reduce font size/margins rather than bunching text.
